# the receiver `table` (book §10; REVIEW e682d71, P51): unit_s7_prim_cross over its own convert.lm2 whose
# table writes `colums:` for `columns:` before `name:` (tests/unit_s7_tbl_posname_table.lm2): a frame
# whose head names no formal binds by position, to `name`, so the real `name:` is said to give it again --
# "the argument name of table is given by position (colums:) and again by name".

fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
